<title>BRAZIL: Brazil 1997/98 coffee crop 22.10 mln bags - Wolthers.</title>
<headline>Brazil 1997/98 coffee crop 22.10 mln bags - Wolthers.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop should total 22.10 million 60-kg bags, said Santos brokers Wolthers and Associates in its second crop estimate.</p>
<p>Previously the company had estimated the crop at 22 million.</p>
<p>The new total comprises arabica output of 17.8 million bags and robusta production of 4.3 million bags.</p>
<p>A breakdown of Wolthers' estimate by state follows.</p>
<p>    STATE					PRODUCTION</p>
<p>					 Arabica	   Robusta</p>
<p> PARANA			    2,500,000</p>
<p> SAO PAULO			 2,700,000</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS		    9,900,000	   100,000</p>
<p> South/West		     (5,700,000)</p>
<p> Cerrado			  (2,300,000)</p>
<p> Zona da Mata		   (1,900,000)	 (100,000)</p>
<p> ESPIRITO SANTO		  1,100,000	 2,500,000</p>
<p> BAHIA				 900,000	   200,000</p>
<p> RONDONIA			    100,000	 1,300,000</p>
<p> OTHERS				600,000	   100,000</p>
<p> TOTAL			    17,800,000	 4,300,000</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
